# Repository contracts

Follow [writing-ai-documents.mdc](writing-ai-documents.mdc). This branch applies to instructions loaded on every turn, such as AGENTS.md; a linked reference does not have the same context cost.

Keep the repo description, authorization boundaries, non-obvious gotchas, and task-triggered pointers in the entry point. Put detailed procedures in the skill or reference that owns them. Use one canonical contract across backends; compatibility entry points should direct the reader there.

Before finishing, check that required references exist, every pointer states when to use it, and no rule conflicts with another loaded instruction. Brevity is useful when it preserves the information needed to act correctly.
